  "note": "Election of the Limavady Urban District Council, polled 15 January 1929; twelve candidates for nine seats (Londonderry Sentinel, 17 January 1929, p. 2). Four retiring councillors and eight new candidates stood. Bloomfield and Kane were described as independents; the other six new candidates (John Hunter, B. M. Hunter, Love, Quigley, Sherrard and Smyth) stood as a joint 'Big Six' slate without a party label. Seventy-five per cent of electors voted; six spoiled votes."
